{
  "baseline": "58bea36f",
  "scope": "First-party WCAFF2 rule-header reader and bounded index for compact and text dictionary stems. Exact stem comparisons after fingerprint filtering preserve dictionary membership. Source assets and spelling rules keep their original provenance.",
  "reference": "https://github.com/hunspell/hunspell/blob/v1.7.5/man/hunspell.5",
  "method": "The current affix_interchange driver was compiled against each reader. The source checker, compact writer and reader were interchanged across 75 published language packs, 24 rule combinations and 12 entry/alias cases. Each writer produced identical bytes on each accepted input. Independently specified valid compact headers and damaged records were also consumed directly. The 24 previously documented differences from external Hunspell and three archives requiring count corrections in the external reference copy were retained.",
  "timingMethod": "Four published dictionaries in optimized binaries. Take the first word from every floor(i*n/128)th valid unflagged-or-flagged alphabetic source word (3 to 20 characters), for i=0..127, and append a second probe suffixed zzq. Run this ordered list 24 times per sample under the in-process lookup clock. One warmup and eight alternating pairs. Compact opening also includes process launch and decompression, with seven alternating pairs. UOS was pinned to CPU 3. Index storage counts element bytes for bucket offsets, row numbers, and tags; it excludes allocator overhead and the shared stem pool.",
